# gpt-oss-120b merge sweep -- BACKFILL QUEUE, consumed one line at a time by
# env/common/wave_backfill.sh as live arms finish and slots open up.
#
# Round 1 launches the _a replicate of each threshold. This queue holds _b and _c,
# taking every threshold to n=3 -- matching the terra b3 design.
#
# ORDER IS ROUND-ROBIN BY THRESHOLD, not grouped: if the queue never fully drains,
# every threshold gets its 2nd replicate before any gets its 3rd. Grouping would
# leave one threshold at n=1 and another at n=3.
#
# The daemon assigns each arm to whichever GPU currently has FEWER live arms, so
# placement stays even without being pinned here.
#
# tag          | context-mode | extra flags
merge_sim085_b | truncation   | --skill-merging --skill-merge-similarity 0.85
merge_sim075_b | truncation   | --skill-merging --skill-merge-similarity 0.75
merge_sim095_b | truncation   | --skill-merging --skill-merge-similarity 0.95
merge_sim085_c | truncation   | --skill-merging --skill-merge-similarity 0.85
merge_sim075_c | truncation   | --skill-merging --skill-merge-similarity 0.75
merge_sim095_c | truncation   | --skill-merging --skill-merge-similarity 0.95
